RETAIL TRADE
Services of Retailers
Classification of Retailers
Small size
Size-Retailers differ in size from small stores to big
departmental store. Some customers prefer to visit large retail
houses to get a wide variety under one roof whereas some
prefer small shops in their local area.
Product Mix- The stores keeping a wide range of different
lines of products are called general stores or departmental
stores whereas stores dealing with one line of products are
known as single line or speciality stores.
Pricing- Some retailers sell goods at fixed price, some permit
bargaining. Some stores located in the market charge a high
price as they add a big profit margin to cover the cost of
maintaining showroem whereas some stores located in
residential areas charge a very nominal price.
