I ITINERANTS
Itinerants refer to retailers who have no fixed place of sale. They move from
one place to another in search of customers They are also known as mobile
vendors. Itinerants deal in low price, daily use items, non-standard items.
Itinerants can further be classified into the following categories:
Hawkers and Pedlars - Hawkers and pedlars move from street
to street in search of customers. A hawker carries the goods
on wheeled carts or on the back of animals and a pedlar
carries the goods on his own head or back.
They move from street to street, in buses, trains, etc. in
search of customers.
They sell a variety of goods such as fruits, vegetables,
toys, bangles, etc.
They deal with non-branded and local items.
They supply the goods at the doorstep of the customer.
The prices are fixed according to the bargaining between
customer and hawkers or pedlars.
